## 🚧 v4.2.0 (Unreleased) — Vault ↔ index sync reconciliation

On `feature/vault-sync-reconcile` (off `feature/spec-vault-sync-reconcile`). Spec:
`docs/specs/SPEC-vault-sync-reconcile-2026-06-26.md`; plan: `ORCHESTRATE-vault-sync-reconcile.md`.
Closes the vault↔DB sync gaps. Not yet released; targets v4.2.0.

- **`obs scan --prune` / `--no-prune`** (S1/S2) — opt-in mark-and-sweep that reconciles the
  index with disk: after scanning, rows whose path is gone (deleted/renamed notes) are swept,
  cascading to links/tags/graph-metrics/embeddings. Default stays additive (`--no-prune`);
  a scan that sees zero files skips the sweep with a warning (bad-path / unmaterialised-iCloud
  guard, no wipe). MCP `rescan_vault` gains the same opt-in `prune=False` parameter.
- **Embedding-cache preservation (N1) + content-hash short-circuit (N2)** — each `obs scan`
  used to re-insert every note unconditionally, and the row replace's `ON DELETE CASCADE`
  wiped each note's `note_embeddings` row (full recompute, latency + paid-API cost, next AI op).
  The scanner now compares each file's `content_hash` against the stored one and skips unchanged
  notes, preserving embeddings/links/tags.
- **Scan-error visibility (S4)** — a note that failed to parse/insert was swallowed by
  `except Exception: continue` while `complete_scan` hardcoded an error count of 0. Failures are
  now counted, captured (path + exception), logged, and surfaced in the scan summary and
  `scan_history`; the scan still completes. Summary now also reports unchanged/pruned/failed counts.
- **`obs doctor --layer sync` (S5)** — new per-vault sync layer with content-based (not just
  time-based) drift: `sync-ghosts`, `sync-missing`, `sync-errors`, and a `sync-drift` summary.
- Tests: full suite green (511 passed / 41 skipped) incl. unit + e2e `TestE2ESyncLifecycle`
  (gated under `E2E=1`) + doctor sync dogfood. Docs: changelog `[Unreleased]`, CLI reference,
  man page, MCP_README, troubleshooting.

