## ✅ v4.0.0 (2026-06-22) — nexus-cli absorption (Phase 1) + MCP vault-resolution correctness + doctor guard

- **Bug A (exact-ID-only resolver):** 9 MCP tools (`get_vault_stats`, `get_hub_notes`, `get_orphaned_notes`, `get_broken_links`, `analyze_vault`, `list_notes`, `create_note`, `rescan_vault`, `diagnose`) resolved vaults with exact-ID-only `db.get_vault()` → a vault **name** or prefix silently returned "Vault not found" (or a misleading empty result). Now route through a `_resolve_vault()` helper wrapping `db.get_vault_by_name_or_id()` (name → exact ID → unambiguous prefix); canonical `id` reassigned before downstream calls. Research tools (`unified_search`/`zotero_*`/`pdf_*`/`course_*`/`manuscript_*`) take no `vault_id` and were unaffected.
- **Bug B (`rescan_vault` no-op):** shelled to the read-only `obs stats` subcommand — reported success while never scanning. Now does a real in-process `vault_manager.scan_vault(path, name)`.
- **Pre-existing doctor crash fixed:** `core/doctor.py` read a non-existent `last_scan` column (schema is `last_scanned`) → `obs doctor` `IndexError` on any real vault. A fake-schema unit test had masked it.
- **New doctor check `mcp-tool-resolvers`** (mcp layer): AST-scans `mcp_server.py`, fails if any `@mcp.tool` uses exact-ID-only `db.get_vault(<param>)`. Catches the bug class automatically.
- **Tests:** 314 unit + 113 MCP unit (research-inclusive; + TestVaultResolution name/prefix coverage, rescan Bug-B guard, 7 doctor AST-guard tests). Full suite green: 426 passed, 33 skipped.

