## 📄 obs man page (2026-06-05) — ✅ MERGED + SHIPPED in v3.2.2 (PR #25 → dev, tap #110/#111)

Cross-repo handoff from flow-cli (which dropped its `obs.1` — it doesn't own the binary). Implements `SPEC-obs-man-page-2026-06-04.md`.

- **`man/man1/obs.1`** — first man page in this repo. Single comprehensive page for the v3.2.1 surface, built from the `src/obs.zsh` dispatch table (not `obs help`). Modeled on flow-cli `g.1`; mandoc lint clean.
- **Help backfill** — added `ai merge-suggest`/`tag-suggest`/`quality` to `obs help --all` (were dispatched but undocumented; help and man page now agree).
- **`install.sh`** — symlinks the page into `$XDG_DATA_HOME/man/man1` with a MANPATH hint.
- **`.TH` version-sync guard** — `__tests__/man-page-version-sync.test.js` asserts the `.TH` product/version track `package.json` (hard CI gate against drift). Date is ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`, mandoc-clean, intentionally unguarded.
- **`--json`/`--verbose` bug fix** — review of the man page surfaced that these *global* argparse flags were appended *after* the subcommand by the zsh `merge-suggest`/`tag-suggest`/`quality` handlers, so `obs_cli.py` rejected them ("unrecognized arguments"). Handlers now route global flags ahead of the `ai` token; 4 regression tests added (Jest 65 → 69). Now the man-page-documented `--json` actually works.
- **Version-bump checklist** — `man/man1/obs.1` added to `.claude/rules/workflows.md` so future bumps move the `.TH` version (now CI-enforced).
- **Homebrew `man1.install`** — ✅ merged (tap PR #110, conditional `if exist?`, install-safe). No-op on the v3.2.1 tarball (predates the page); fires automatically once an obs release bundles `man/man1/obs.1`. That release is the remaining runtime gate for `man obs` from a brew install.

